  "Question": "If\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} (7+4\\sqrt3)x^2 &+(2+\\sqrt3)x\\\\ &-2=0, \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nthe larger root minus the smaller root is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2+3\\sqrt3\\)",
    "B": "\\(2-\\sqrt3\\)",
    "C": "\\(6+3\\sqrt3\\)",
    "D": "\\(6-3\\sqrt3\\)",
    "E": "\\(3\\sqrt3+2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The leading coefficient is the square of the linear coefficient:\n\\[\n(2+\\sqrt3)^2=7+4\\sqrt3.\n\\]\nLet \\(u=2+\\sqrt3\\), so \\(u>0\\). Treating \\(ux\\) as one quantity turns the equation into\n\\[\n(ux)^2+ux-2=0,\n\\qquad (ux-1)(ux+2)=0.\n\\]\nBecause \\(u\\ne0\\), the two roots are \\(\\frac1u\\) and \\(-\\frac2u\\). The first is larger since \\(u>0\\), so their difference is\n\\[\n\\frac1u-\\left(-\\frac2u\\right)\n=\\frac3{2+\\sqrt3}\n=\\frac{3(2-\\sqrt3)}{4-3}\n=6-3\\sqrt3.\n\\]\nTherefore the answer is choice D.",
